<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-only
  Copyright (c) 2026 the Appname contributors

  macOS hardened-runtime entitlements — allow-jit ARM (ES §33.4 macOS row,
  ES:10961; §25.3 plugin sandbox; §48.3 Wasmtime CVE note ES:17067).

  THE MINIMAL SET, and nothing else. The single entitlement
  com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit exists ONLY for a build whose shipped
  dylib contains the Wasmtime sandboxed plugin tier (feature `wasm-plugins`
  in appname-script): a Cranelift JIT needs writable-then-executable pages,
  which the hardened runtime forbids without this entitlement.

  WHICH VARIANT A BUILD GETS IS MEASURED, NOT ASSUMED. scripts/build_dmg.sh
  reads the shipped dylib and selects this file only when wasmtime/cranelift
  symbols are present, else the no-jit variant; the entitlement surface
  therefore tracks the compiled-in tier, which is §48.3's "disabling the
  tier shrinks the entitlement surface".

  STATE OF THE 1.0 BUILD, measured on RC0's artifact (OB-95, operator WORD
  14 ruling 3): the shipped libappname_cabi.dylib carries NO wasmtime and no
  cranelift symbols, because crates/appname-cabi/Cargo.toml takes
  appname-script with its default features turned off. RC0 was therefore
  signed with the no-jit variant and an EMPTY entitlement set. An earlier
  version of this comment asserted the opposite as "verified", and was false
  against the artifact for as long as it stood. This file is kept for a
  build that compiles the tier back in.

  Deliberately ABSENT (ES:10961 "and nothing else"):
    * com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation — NOT granted; every
      bundled dylib is signed with the same Developer ID (LGPL Qt frameworks
      via macdeployqt included). Library validation stays on.
    * allow-unsigned-executable-memory / allow-dyld-environment-variables /
      any network or device entitlement — none; the app's network posture is
      the §25.3/§30.1 in-process gate, not an OS entitlement.
-->
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
